 "notes": [
  "Hiphil's sole citation (2Sam.20.5, \"vayyocher min-hammoed\", \"he was late/tarried beyond the appointed time\") shows Amasa's own tardiness (an intransitive \"delay\", matching qal/piel), not a transitive \"hinder [someone else] / keep [someone else] back\" -- neither current clause is a clean fit. Kept \"keep back\" (dropping \"hinder\" as the redundant synonym) since it stretches more naturally to a passive/intransitive reading, but this stem's gloss may be worth reconsidering entirely."
